    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2KfDarRgEMrYDqCkbJatwoc)_\n\nNew module `sp-vault-perf` (doc `docs/tangles/text/sp-vault-perf.org`, loaded right after `sp-org-base`):\n\n- `read-process-output-max` 1 MB (the background vulpea scan reads its file list from a subprocess).\n- `bidi-paragraph-direction` left-to-right, `bidi-inhibit-bpa`, `inhibit-compacting-font-caches`, `global-so-long-mode`.\n- `org-agenda-inhibit-startup`, and the Org element cache pinned on.\n- `M-x sp-vault-perf-report`: file count, vulpea.db size, org-id table size, agenda files, GC count and time.\n\n**Left out on purpose:** `gc-cons-threshold`, gcmh/idle GC and the autosync delay (the vterm work may change them).\n\n**Not checked:** not run in Emacs (none in the container); the effect on the hang is not measured. Tangle output was built by script, so the `tangle` check is the real test.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCrZBo9FdSD2av1b75)_",
